{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Learning.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Learning.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unsupervised learning unsupervised learning","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Learning.md","fileName":"Unsupervised Learning.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unsupervised Learning","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 16:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Neural Network Training]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Training Dataset","Supervised Learning","Autoencoder","aiassistants.epub","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Learning.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Learning.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unsupervised learning unsupervised learning","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Learning.md","fileName":"Unsupervised Learning.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unsupervised Learning","heading":"Unsupervised Learning","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Unsupervised learning searches for structure in data without being given target labels. It can group similar examples, discover recurring patterns, or learn compact representations that later support another task.\n\nBecause no answer key is supplied, the discovered structure is not automatically equivalent to a human concept. The method is nevertheless valuable when unlabeled data are abundant and annotated [[Training Dataset|training datasets]] are scarce.\n\nClustering illustrates the setup: observations are supplied without correct group assignments, so the algorithm must derive a useful organization from the inputs themselves. This contrasts with [[Supervised Learning]], where desired outputs guide every training example.\n\nKelleher also describes [[Autoencoder|autoencoders]] as a way to learn a representation by reconstructing inputs without task labels. Such representations can later support a supervised model. The book presents increased interest in these methods partly as a response to the expense of annotating ever larger datasets, not as a guarantee that unlabeled learning always replaces labeled evaluation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Training Dataset","Supervised Learning","Autoencoder","aiassistants.epub","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Learning.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Learning.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unsupervised learning unsupervised learning","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Learning.md","fileName":"Unsupervised Learning.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unsupervised Learning","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiassistants.epub]]\n\n[[algorithms.epub]]\n\n[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Training Dataset","Supervised Learning","Autoencoder","aiassistants.epub","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}